1. Definitions

"Software" means the source code, object code, and other copyrightable material
in this repository that Starfall Org owns or is authorized to license under
these terms.

"Official Repository" means the repository maintained by Starfall Org from
which this License is distributed.

"Qualifying Code Contribution" means a contribution that:

(a) changes program source code, tests, build logic, or other technical code;
(b) is submitted under an identity attributable to a natural person or legal
    entity;
(c) is accepted by the maintainers and merged into the Official Repository;
    and
(d) is not solely documentation, translation, issue reporting, discussion,
    review, sponsorship, formatting, generated metadata, or another
    non-code-only contribution.

An automated or bot account does not independently become a Contributor. A
natural person or legal entity using automation may qualify only when the
Qualifying Code Contribution is attributable to that person or entity.

"Contributor" means:

(a) a natural person who has made at least one Qualifying Code Contribution; or
(b) a legal entity on whose behalf at least one Qualifying Code Contribution
    was made, provided the entity owns or controls the copyright in that
    contribution or the contributor was authorized to submit it on the
    entity's behalf.

An individual's contribution does not automatically make that individual's
employer, client, or affiliated organization a Contributor unless paragraph
(b) applies. Contributor status is not transferable or sublicensable.

"Commercial Use" means use of the Software primarily intended for or directed
toward commercial advantage, business operations, or monetary compensation,
including internal business use, paid products or services, advertising-funded
products or services, paid hosting, consulting, integration, support, or other
revenue-generating activity.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form of the Software for making
modifications, including the scripts and project files reasonably required to
build the distributed object code, but excluding generally available system
libraries and tools used unmodified.

2. General Non-Commercial Permission

Subject to this License, any person or entity may, for Non-Commercial purposes:

(a) use and run the Software;
(b) inspect, study, copy, and modify the Software; and
(c) redistribute the Software or modified versions of it, in source or object
    form, provided all requirements in Sections 4 through 7 are satisfied.

No Commercial Use is permitted under this Section.

3. Contributor Commercial Permission

A Contributor may use, run, modify, reproduce, and redistribute the Software
for Commercial Use, subject to all other terms of this License.

The Contributor commercial permission:

(a) begins when the Qualifying Code Contribution is merged into the Official
    Repository;
(b) applies to the Contributor identified in Section 1, not automatically to
    employers, clients, parents, subsidiaries, affiliates, customers, or other
    third parties;
(c) does not transfer to a recipient merely because the recipient obtains the
    Software from a Contributor; and
(d) does not remove the copyleft, source-availability, notice, or attribution
    obligations in this License.

Starfall Org, as licensor, may use the Software commercially and may grant
separate permissions to the extent it owns or controls the relevant rights.

4. Copyleft for Modified Versions

If you redistribute a modified version of the Software, you must:

(a) clearly state that you modified the Software and identify the date of the
    modification;
(b) license the entire modified work, to the extent it is based on the
    Software, under this same License;
(c) keep all copyright, authorship, attribution, and license notices intact;
    and
(d) not impose additional terms that restrict a recipient from exercising the
    permissions this License grants to that recipient.

You may not relicense the Software or a derivative work under a different
license unless every relevant copyright holder has separately authorized that
relicensing.

5. Distribution of Source Code

You may redistribute source code only if you provide a complete copy of this
License with it and satisfy Section 4.

6. Distribution of Object Code

If you redistribute object code, including an application package or other
binary form, you must also make the Corresponding Source available to every
recipient at no additional charge, using one of these methods:

(a) accompany the object code with the Corresponding Source; or
(b) provide a clear, durable network location from which the recipient may
    obtain the Corresponding Source for at least three years after your last
    distribution of that object-code version.

The Corresponding Source must be provided under this same License.

7. No Removal of Recipient Conditions

Redistribution does not grant a recipient Contributor status. A recipient who
is not independently a Contributor may exercise only the non-commercial rights
in Section 2, even when the Software was distributed by a Contributor in a
commercial transaction.

You may charge for copies, hosting, support, or services only if you are a
Contributor or have separate written commercial permission from the relevant
copyright holders. Charging a recipient does not itself grant that recipient
Commercial Use rights.

8. Network Use

Running a modified or unmodified copy of the Software to provide a network
service, without distributing a copy of the Software, does not by itself
trigger the source-distribution requirements in Sections 4 through 6.

However, operating such a service for Commercial Use still requires Contributor
status or separate written commercial permission under Section 3.

9. Contributions

A contribution is licensed under this License when its copyright holder submits
it for inclusion in the Official Repository with knowledge that the repository
uses this License, unless the maintainers and contributor expressly agree in
writing to different terms.

Nothing in this Section transfers ownership of a contribution to Starfall Org.
A contributor must have the legal right to submit the contribution.

